    "number": 239,
    "title": "refactor: extract budget config validation",
    "body": "# Closes #212\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR refactors the budget configuration handling in the CLI by consolidating the duplicated validation/loading logic into a shared helper. The change reduces code duplication, improves maintainability, and keeps the existing behavior intact.\r\n\r\n## What Changed\r\n\r\n- Extracted the budget config parsing/validation flow into a dedicated helper function.\r\n- Updated the CLI entry point to use the shared helper instead of repeating the same logic inline.\r\n- Added unit tests covering:\r\n  - missing config paths\r\n  - valid TOML input\r\n  - invalid TOML input\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nThe previous implementation repeated the same validation logic in the entry path, which increased maintenance overhead and made the behavior harder to evolve consistently. Centralizing this logic makes the code easier to read and less prone to divergence.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\r\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\r\n- `cargo test --workspace`\r\n\r\n",
